This product is a desktop port of the DeepSeek Harness web application and
distributes software derived from it.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. Upstream-derived client (shipped inside the installer)
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
DeepSeek Harness (upstream project: deepseek-ai/deepseek-harness)
Pinned upstream commit: 687f282e8625c6b8d11ff58211a90524be2e4317 (0.2.1-rc.2)
Licensed under the MIT License. Copyright (c) 2026 DeepSeek.

The desktop installer ships the upstream web client, built with upstream's
own official build profile, under port/runtime-payload/dsh/. The runtime payload
is generated at build time from a reference checkout of the upstream repository
and is NOT tracked in this source repository. The upstream MIT license text
governs that payload and is reproduced in the LICENSE file at the root of this
repository.

The port also applies a small, version-pinned set of source patches to the
emitted client and host bundles for account integration and Settings > Updates.
Those patched files remain upstream-derived and are governed by the same MIT
license.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. Bundled Node.js runtime
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
Node.js 22.20.0 (Linux/macOS/Windows x64 + arm64)
https://nodejs.org/dist/v22.20.0/
Licensed under the MIT License. Copyright (c) OpenJS Foundation and other
contributors.

The pinned interpreter is staged from the official nodejs.org archive whose
SHA-256 digest is declared in port/installer/node-runtime.json. The archive's
license text is copied into the payload as NODE-LICENSE.txt by
port/scripts/lib/node-runtime.psm1 and is verified to be present, non-empty
and non-symlinked by port/scripts/lib/seal-runtime.mjs.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. Third-party components
--------------------------------------------------------------------------
The runtime payload bundles its dependency closure, whose packages retain
their own license files in place under the payload's node_modules tree.
Refer to each package's own license terms.
